lisa-design:
- Accounts mode = aws_accounts set: one evalScope per listed account, sequentially, in config order, under <root>/acct-<id>; nothing runs with ambient credentials unless the hub is listed with use_ambient_credentials. Regions per account: entry regions > aws_regions > all (empty); a Warn per account scanning all regions (c7n enumerates regions with the hub's credentials, aws.py:784); only a warning (user decision).
- Every account in accounts mode (ambient too) uses its own cache file and exports C7N_SESSION_SUFFIX and CCF_CUSTODIAN_ACCOUNT_ID; only role accounts get --assume/--external-id.
- Identity (accounts mode only): account_id label = scanned account, overriding resource data (records and payloads); account_name label when the entry has a name; payload.account {id, name} (name always present) and resource.account_id; subject id cloud-custodian-resource/<account>/<type>/<id> (still SUBJECT_TYPE_RESOURCE); Init identity keys [provider, account_id, resource_type, resource_id], templates stay COMPONENT; baselines are per scope, never merged across accounts. policy_labels account_id/account_name are dropped (reserved, same semantics as the existing reserved labels) with a Configure warning.
- Failure (user decision): c7n exit 1 with "Unable to assume role" (commands.py) marks the account; its remaining baselines/checks are skipped and counted. Any account with an execution failure is recorded; other accounts still run and their evidence is flushed at the end of each account. Eval then returns FAILURE with formatAccountFailures: first line names every failed account ("cloud custodian failed in N of M AWS account(s): <id> (<name)> [could not assume role], ...; evidence from the other K account(s) was submitted"), then per account its role, the first 2 KiB of its errors and the stderr/custodian-run.log tails of its failed runs (16 KiB per account, 128 KiB total, omitted accounts counted). The agent receives it as the gRPC status message (rpc error: code = Unknown desc = ...): logged as "Error running plugin" and stored as the plugin error artifact of the agent run evidence (1 MiB cap); the gRPC header limit is 16 MiB.
- Non-fatal policy evaluation errors of a successful account keep today's semantics (warn, SUCCESS) and are prefixed with the account. Policy entries that don't parse are reported once, not per account. Zero evidence across all accounts without an account failure uses today's composeZeroEvidenceError, with diagnostics named <account>/<run>.
- Beyond the spec: Configure rejects non-AWS policies in accounts mode (accounts and roles only mean something to AWS policies; running a gcp policy once per AWS account would duplicate it).
